  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "On the mountain waist of San Cha Mountain, as a Zuo versus Che fight nears its end, elder Zuo Wu Sheng stands wounded before her and tells Big Missy to leave while the elders block the enemy. Narration calls her the future hope of Zuo clan, young and pretty, and says the clan cannot afford her death here. She answers with hesitation and dismay.",
      "chapters": [
        323
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "intro",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt",
      "mentions": [
        "loc_san_cha_mountain",
        "char_zuo_wu_sheng",
        "fac_zuo_clan"
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "She is young and pretty.",
      "chapters": [
        323
      ],
      "certainty": "canon",
      "confidence": "B",
      "verification": "cross_checked_chapter_summary",
      "source_id": "src_sagaofgu",
      "section": "appearance",
      "text_origin": "source_excerpt"
    },
    {
      "text": "When Kong Ri Tian appears, her face goes pale with the other fighters. During the chaotic petal and butterfly assault she and Che Qiao Xiang fall unconscious and are taken in his hands. Zuo Wu Sheng cries out for Chan Yu as Kong Ri Tian gloats over the two captives, then the three kings inheritance pillars erupt and even he forgets the women in his arms.",
